  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In $\\mathrm{KO}_2$, the nature of oxygen species and the oxidation state of oxygen atom are superoxide (superoxide ion is $\\mathrm{O}_2^{-}$) and $-1 / 2$ respectively.\nLet $x$ be oxidation state of oxygen. The oxidation state of $\\mathrm{K}$ is $+1$. Hence\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\n+1+2(x)=0 \\\\\n2 x=-1 \\\\\nx=-\\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{gathered}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
